       1.7.1 AS-REP Roasting Vulnerability Analysis - (completed) {Findings: Kerberos preauthentication is a security feature in Microsoft's Active Directory that protects user accounts from offline password cracking attacks. It requires the client to demonstrate knowledge of their password before a Ticket Granting Ticket (TGT) is issued. AS-REP Roasting is a technique exploited when the "Do not require Kerberos preauthentication" option is enabled for a user account. The steps involved in AS-REP Roasting include identification of vulnerable accounts, requesting AS-REP, hash extraction, and offline cracking. The impact of AS-REP Roasting can lead to unauthorized access, privilege escalation, lateral movement, and data exfiltration. Reasons for disabling preauthentication often relate to compatibility with older Kerberos versions, specific applications or services not supporting Kerberos preauthentication, or troubleshooting account lockout issues. svc-alfresco account do not require Kerberos preauthentication.}
