1.2. Identify running services [completed]: {Findings: Target is Windows domain controller. Domain: breach.vl, Hostname: BREACHDC, OS: Windows Server 2022 Build 20348. SMB signing required. Clock synchronized within 5 seconds.}
2. Service Enumeration [completed]
2.1. Enumerate SMB for anonymous access [completed]: {Findings: Guest account has READ access to Users and IPC$ shares. Guest account has READ/WRITE access to share named 'share'. RID brute force revealed 10 domain users: Claire.Pope, Julia.Wong, Hilary.Reed, Diana.Pope, Jasmine.Price, George.Williams, Lawrence.Kaur, Jasmine.Slater, Hugh.Watts, Christine.Bruce. One service account found: svc_mssql. Username format: first.last. Share 'share' contains three subdirectories: finance (empty), software (empty), transfer (contains three user folders: claire.pope, diana.pope, julia.wong - guest cannot list inside these).}
2.2. Enumerate HTTP service [completed]: {Findings: IIS 10.0 default page. Directory brute force found no hidden directories or files. No useful content discovered on web service.}
3. Initial Access [completed]
3.1. Capture NetNTLMv2 hash via SMB lure files [completed]: {Findings: Captured NetNTLMv2 hash for user Julia.Wong: Julia.Wong::BREACH:a1905663fa6d011b:859D2DC6D8872075FC28AF6FCDEBD0A2:}
3.2. Crack NetNTLMv2 hash [completed]: {Findings: Password cracked successfully: Julia.Wong:Computer1. Credentials validated via SMB - authentication successful. User does not have WinRM or RDP access. User flag found in SMB share at \\share\transfer\julia.wong\user.txt}
4. Domain Enumeration [completed]
4.1. Enumerate Active Directory with BloodHound [completed]: {Findings: BloodHound data collected successfully. Domain SID: S-1-5-21-2330692793-3312915120-706255856. Julia.Wong has no interesting outbound control or privilege escalation paths. One Kerberoastable user identified: svc_mssql. Service account has SPN: MSSQLSvc/breachdc.breach.vl:1433 indicating it runs the MSSQL service.}
4.2. Identify privilege escalation paths [completed]: {Findings: No direct privilege escalation from Julia.Wong. Kerberoastable account svc_mssql identified as attack vector.}
5. Kerberoasting [completed]
5.1. Extract Kerberoast hash for svc_mssql [completed]: {Findings: TGS hash extracted: $krb5tgs$23$*svc_mssql$BREACH.VL$breach.vl\svc_mssql*$8a00486bd5075b4f5d8618b1488d7b9a$...}
5.2. Crack Kerberoast hash [completed]: {Findings: Password cracked: svc_mssql:Trustno1. Credentials validated via SMB. Account does not have WinRM or RDP access. Both Julia.Wong and svc_mssql can connect to MSSQL service on port 1433, but both map to guest account with no sysadmin privileges.}
6. MSSQL Privilege Escalation [completed]
6.1. Forge silver ticket for MSSQL service [completed]: {Findings: NTLM hash calculated: 69596c7aa1e8daee17f8e78870e25a5c. Silver ticket forged as Administrator using ticketer.py with parameters: -nthash 69596c7aa1e8daee17f8e78870e25a5c -domain-sid S-1-5-21-2330692793-3312915120-706255856 -domain breach.vl -spn MSSQLSvc/breachdc.breach.vl:1433. Connected to MSSQL as BREACH\Administrator with sysadmin privileges (dbo role). Login enumeration shows Administrator, NT SERVICE\SQLWriter, NT SERVICE\Winmgmt, and NT Service\MSSQL$SQLEXPRESS all have sysadmin role.}
6.2. Research silver ticket attack [completed]: {Findings: Silver ticket is forged Kerberos TGS using service account password hash. Requirements: NTLM hash of service password (calculate from Trustno1), domain SID (S-1-5-21-2330692793-3312915120-706255856 from BloodHound), SPN (MSSQLSvc/breachdc.breach.vl:1433), target username (Administrator likely has sysadmin). Use Impacket ticketer.py to forge ticket.}
7. Code Execution as svc_mssql [completed]
7.1. Enable xp_cmdshell on MSSQL [completed]: {Findings: xp_cmdshell enabled successfully using enable_xp_cmdshell command. Configuration option changed from 0 to 1.}
7.2. Test command execution [completed]: {Findings: Command execution verified. 'xp_cmdshell whoami' returns breach\svc_mssql. Privileges enumeration shows SeImpersonatePrivilege enabled, SeAssignPrimaryTokenPrivilege disabled, SeManageVolumePrivilege enabled.}
